});
```

---

## Credentials Handling

### Before - ❌ WRONG
```
.env.test file committed to repository
Contains:
- Database passwords
- AWS access keys
- API tokens
- Production credentials

Anyone can access them!
```

### After - ✅ CORRECT
```
.gitignore prevents commits:
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

.env.example provided:
Contains template values
No real credentials

Separate per-environment configs:
development: .env.development
testing: .env.test (local only)
production: AWS Secrets Manager
```

---

## Performance & Monitoring

### Before
```
No monitoring
No logging
No visibility into errors
Crashes cause data loss
```

### After
```javascript
// Request logging
app.use(morgan('combined'));

// Error logging with context
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error({
    timestamp: new Date().toISOString(),
    error: err.message,
    status: err.status,
    path: req.path,
    method: req.method
  });
});

// Graceful shutdown
process.on('SIGTERM', () => {
  server.close(() => process.exit(0));
});
```

---

## Summary Table

