# Quick Fix Guide: Hardcoded Values

## 🚨 Issues Found: 3 Hardcoded Values

### Issue 1: Hardcoded Port (3000)
**File:** app.js:18  
**Severity:** 🟡 MEDIUM  
**Fix Time:** 5 minutes

```javascript
// ❌ BEFORE
app.listen(3000, () => {
  console.log('Server running on port 3000');
});

// ✅ AFTER
const PORT = parseInt(process.env.PORT || '3000', 10);
const HOST = process.env.HOST || 'localhost';
app.listen(PORT, HOST, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on ${HOST}:${PORT}`);
});
```

**Add to .env:**
```bash
PORT=3000
HOST=localhost
```

---

### Issue 2: Test Data with Exposed Emails
**File:** app.js:13-14  
**Severity:** 🔵 LOW  
**Fix Time:** 10 minutes

```javascript
// ❌ BEFORE
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', email: 'bob@example.com' },
  ]);
});

// ✅ AFTER
app.get('/users', (req, res) => {
  // Only return if authorized
  const includeEmail = process.env.RETURN_USER_EMAIL === 'true';
  res.json([
    { id: 1, name: 'Alice', ...(includeEmail && { email: 'alice@example.com' }) },
    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', ...(includeEmail && { email: 'bob@example.com' }) }
  ]);
});
```

**Add to .env:**
```bash
RETURN_USER_EMAIL=false
```

